b2 + D(a + 1/2) + E o_y = 0\n\nRecall that o_y = (2a + 1) h / (2(a + 1))\n\nLet me compute each term in equation (2):\n\nFirst term: (a + 1/2)^2 = a\u00b2 + a + 1/4\n\nSecond term: o_y\u00b2 = [ (2a + 1)^2 h\u00b2 ] / [4(a + 1)^2 ]\n\nThird term: D(a + 1/2)\n\nFourth term: E o_y = E * (2a + 1) h / (2(a + 1))\n\nSo equation (2) becomes:\n\na\u00b2 + a + 1/4 + [ (2a + 1)^2 h\u00b2 ] / [4(a + 1)^2 ] + D(a + 1/2) + E * (2a + 1) h / (2(a + 1)) = 0\n\nMultiply all terms by 4(a + 1)^2 to eliminate denominators:\n\n4(a + 1)^2 (a\u00b2 + a + 1/4) + (2a + 1)^2 h\u00b2 + 4(a + 1)^2 D(a + 1/2) + 2(a + 1)(2a + 1) E h = 0\n\nThis seems very complicated. Let's see if we can substitute h\u00b2 = 1 - a\u00b2 (since AB = 1) and express everything in terms of a.\n\nFirst term: 4(a + 1)^2 (a\u00b2 + a + 1/4)\n\nLet me compute this:\n\nFirst, expand (a + 1)^2 = a\u00b2 + 2a + 1\n\nMultiply by (a\u00b2 + a + 1/4):\n\n(a\u00b2 + 2a + 1)(a\u00b2 + a + 1/4) = a\u00b2(a\u00b2 + a + 1/4) + 2a(a\u00b2 + a + 1/4) + 1(a\u00b2 + a + 1/4)\n\n= a^4 + a^3 + (1/4)a\u00b2 + 2a^3 + 2a\u00b2 + (1/2)a + a\u00b2 + a + 1/4\n\nCombine like terms:\n\na^4 + (a^3 + 2a^3) + ( (1/4)a\u00b2 + 2a\u00b2 + a\u00b2 ) + ( (1/2)a + a ) + 1/4\n\n= a^4 + 3a^3 + ( (1/4 + 2 + 1 )a\u00b2 ) + ( 3/2 a ) + 1/4\n\n= a^4 + 3a^3 + (13/4 a\u00b2) + (3/2 a) + 1/4\n\nMultiply by 4:\n\n4a^4 + 12a^3 + 13a\u00b2 + 6a + 1\n\nSecond term: (2a + 1)^2 h\u00b2 = (4a\u00b2 + 4a + 1)(1 - a\u00b2) = (4a\u00b2 + 4a + 1)(1 - a\u00b2)\n\nExpand this:\n\n4a\u00b2(1) + 4a\u00b2(-a\u00b2) + 4a(1) + 4a(-a\u00b2) + 1(1) + 1(-a\u00b2)\n\n= 4a\u00b2 - 4a^4 + 4a - 4a^3 + 1 - a\u00b2\n\nCombine like terms:\n\n-4a^4 -4a^3 + (4a\u00b2 - a\u00b2) + 4a + 1\n\n= -4a^4 -4a^3 + 3a\u00b2 + 4a + 1\n\nThird term: 4(a + 1)^2 D(a + 1/2)\n\nFourth term: 2(a + 1)(2a + 1) E h\n\nNow, from equation (1): D a + E h = - (a\u00b2 + h\u00b2) = - (a\u00b2 + 1 - a\u00b2 ) = -1\n\nSo E h = -1 - D a\n\nThus, E = (-1 - D a)/h\n\nSubstitute into fourth term:\n\n2(a + 1)(2a + 1) * [