rix}\n    $$\n    \n    Compute the determinant:\n    $$\n    \\overrightarrow{M_0 M_1} \\times \\vec{l} = \\left( (y_1 - y_0)p - (z_1 - z_0)n \\right) \\mathbf{i} - \\left( (x_1 - x_0)p - (z_1 - z_0)m \\right) \\mathbf{j} + \\left( (x_1 - x_0)n - (y_1 - y_0)m \\right) \\mathbf{k}\n    $$\n\n6. Find the magnitude of this cross product:\n    $$\n    \\left| \\overrightarrow{M_0 M_1} \\times \\vec{l} \\right| = \\sqrt{ \\left( (y_1 - y_0)p - (z_1 - z_0)n \\right)^2 + \\left( (x_1 - x_0)p - (z_1 - z_0)m \\right)^2 + \\left( (x_1 - x_0)n - (y_1 - y_0)m \\right)^2 }\n    $$\n\n7. Calculate the magnitude of vector $\\vec{l}$:\n    $$\n    |\\vec{l}| = \\sqrt{m^2 + n^2 + p^2}\n    $$\n\n8. Finally, the distance $h$ is:\n    $$\n    h = \\frac{ \\sqrt{ \\left( (y_1 - y_0)p - (z_1 - z_0)n \\right)^2 + \\left( (x_1 - x_0)p - (z_1 - z_0)m \\right)^2 + \\left( (x_1 - x_0)n - (y_1 - y_0)m \\right)^2 } }{ \\sqrt{m^2 + n^2 + p^2} }\n    $$\n\nIn conclusion, the distance from the point $M_1 \\left(x_1, y_1, z_1\\right)$ to the line given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-x_0}{m}=\\frac{y-y_0}{n}=\\frac{z-z0}{p}\n$$\n\nis:\n$$\n\\boxed{ \\frac{ \\sqrt{ \\left( (y_1 - y_0)p - (z_1 - z_0)n \\right)^2 + \\left( (x_1 - x_0)p - (z_1 - z_0)m \\right)^2 + \\left( (x_1 - x_0)n - (y_1 - y_0)m \\right)^2 } }{ \\sqrt{m^2 + n^2 + p^2} } }\n$$", "domain": "math", "source": "numina_math", "test_cases": null, "starter_code": null}, {"problem": "In trapezoid \\(ABCD\\) with bases \\(BC\\) and \\(AD\\), the angle \\(\\angle DAB\\) is right. It is known that there exists a unique point \\(M\\) on side \\(CD\\) such that the angle \\(\\angle BMA\\) is right.\n\nProve that \\(BC = CM\\) and \\(AD = MD\\).", "deepseek_reasoning": "Okay, so I need to prove that in trapezoid \\(ABCD\\) with bases \\(BC\\) and \\(AD\\), where \\(\\angle DAB\\) is a right angle, and there exists a unique point \\(M\\) on side \\(CD\\) such that \\(\\angle BMA\\) is right, then \\(BC = CM\\) and \\(AD = MD\\). Hmm, let me start by visualiz